data: {"sequence_number":156,"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"**The current latest LTS release of Node.js is v26.13.0 (codenamed 'Lithium').**[[1]](https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases)\n\nIt was released on October 28, 2026, marking the transition of the 26.x line into Active LTS status with support through April 2029.[[2]](https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/latest)\n\nThis is confirmed directly on the official Node.js previous releases page (listing v26 as LTS with last update Oct 28, 2026) and the Node.js GitHub releases page (tagging 26.13.0 as the latest LTS).[[1]](https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases)","logprobs":[],"annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases","start_index":80,"end_index":132,"title":"1"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/latest","start_index":266,"end_index":319,"title":"2"},{"type":"url_citation","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases","start_index":519,"end_index":571,"title":"1"}]}],"id":"msg_4f9a964f-1421-9576-97e3-92a342257b27","role":"assistant","type":"message","status":"completed"},"output_index":8}

